---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';
import SelectSaunasButton from '../../components/SelectSaunasButton.astro';

const pinnacleUrl = 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/almost-heaven-pinnacle-morgan-4-person-classic-barrel-sauna-6x6-ft';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Where are Almost Heaven saunas made?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Almost Heaven says it has made saunas in West Virginia's Greenbrier Valley since 1977. Its current lineup also includes a separate Harvia Collection described as crafted in Europe, so verify the country of origin on the exact product page."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do Almost Heaven sauna kits include a heater?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Almost Heaven says an electric heater is standard with every sauna it sells, and most kits use a Harvia KIP sized for the room. Some models offer other electric or wood-burning configurations. Check the selected variant because controls, stones, and heater upgrades can change the package."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does the Almost Heaven warranty cover?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Almost Heaven currently describes a limited lifetime warranty against manufacturing defects on the sauna room. It separately lists one year for heater elements and five years for other heater components. Normal wear, rot, discoloration, and minor lumber splintering are among the stated exclusions."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Base
  title="Almost Heaven Saunas Review: Models, Heaters and Buying Checks"
  description="A source-backed Almost Heaven brand guide covering current barrel and cabin options, heater packages, delivery, warranty, and questions to resolve before buying."
  canonical="/brands/almost-heaven-sauna-review"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-3">Brand decision guide</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Almost Heaven Saunas: what to compare before buying</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-500 mb-8">Last reviewed August 15, 2026</p>

    <div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden mb-3">
      <img src="/images/lifestyle/barrel-sauna-chimney.jpg" alt="Representative outdoor barrel sauna with a chimney" class="w-full object-cover max-h-80" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mb-8">Representative barrel-sauna setting; not a photo of one specific Almost Heaven configuration.</p>

    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>Research scope:</strong> This is a desk-researched brand guide, not a hands-on factory or product test. We checked current manufacturer product pages, support and warranty language, installation details, and an authorized retailer listing. Configurations and availability can change.
    </div>

    <p class="text-lg text-stone-700 mb-4">Almost Heaven is not one barrel sauna repeated in different sizes. Its current catalog spans classic barrels, canopy barrels, indoor rooms, infrared cabins, and a Europe-crafted Harvia Collection. Start with the format and installation plan. Then compare exact configurations.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-8">The brand says it has built saunas in West Virginia's Greenbrier Valley since 1977 and joined the Harvia family in 2019. That relationship matters because current kits use Harvia heater packages, but the heater and controls still vary by model and option.</p>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-9">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Shortlist by project, not by rank</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3 text-stone-700 text-sm">
        <li><strong>Pinnacle:</strong> compact 6-by-6-foot classic barrel with a current 6 kW electric configuration.</li>
        <li><strong>Grandview:</strong> larger canopy barrel with electric and eligible wood-burning configurations; freight and site access need more planning.</li>
        <li><strong>Indoor and Harvia Collection:</strong> cabin-style choices for buyers who do not want a traditional American barrel format.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Pinnacle: the compact barrel reference point</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Almost Heaven currently lists the Pinnacle as a four-person, 6-by-6-foot barrel. The published configuration uses a 6 kW, 240V, 30A hardwired heater and a separate 120V lighting connection. Its 63.25-inch benches are more useful than the capacity label when you judge comfort.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">The product configurator currently offers different lumber, door, window, and heater choices. Confirm which one is in the quoted price and which manuals apply. Do not assume an old Amazon package matches the current direct-sale configuration.</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mb-9">
      <SelectSaunasButton href={pinnacleUrl} label="View current Pinnacle listing" ctaPosition="brand_pinnacle" />
      <a href="/reviews/almost-heaven-pinnacle-review/" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center border border-stone-300 text-stone-800 font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-stone-50">Read the Pinnacle buyer checklist</a>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Grandview: more room and more delivery scope</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">The current Grandview is a 4-to-6-person canopy barrel with a one-foot exterior canopy. Almost Heaven lists 8 or 9 kW electric options and an eligible M3 wood-burning package. The manufacturer also warns that this unit ships by flatbed and publishes an 8-to-12-week lead-time estimate.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">That makes delivery access part of the buying decision. Verify the current packed dimensions, truck requirements, unloading responsibility, route from curb to pad, and damage-reporting deadline before ordering.</p>
    <a href="https://almostheaven.com/products/grandview-4-6-person-canopy-barrel-sauna" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 font-semibold hover:underline">Review the current Grandview configurations</a>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Indoor rooms and the Harvia Collection</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Almost Heaven's catalog now extends beyond its USA-made barrel line. The Harvia Collection is described by the company as crafted in Europe and includes indoor and outdoor cabin designs. Country of origin, construction, heater package, freight, and installation scope can therefore differ across the brand.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">If you are comparing an indoor room with a barrel, do not compare capacity and sale price alone. Compare bench dimensions, insulation, glass area, heater and controls, floor requirements, ventilation plan, delivery, and assembly.</p>
    <a href="https://almostheaven.com/collections/heritage-collection" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 font-semibold hover:underline">Explore the current Harvia Collection</a>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">The heater is part of the configured kit</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Almost Heaven's current FAQ says an electric heater is standard with every sauna it sells and that most kits use a KIP heater sized for the room. Current upgrade options can include KIP manual or digital packages, The Wall, Cilindro, Virta, and Virta Combi. Some larger outdoor models can be configured for wood heat.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">That is different from the old advice to immediately replace the included heater. Instead, compare the exact package: heater item number, controls, sensors, stones, power unit, electrical requirements, clearances, and warranty. Changing heaters later can affect fit, controls, electrical work, and the manufacturer's installation requirements.</p>
    <p class="mb-8"><a href="/brands/harvia-sauna-heater-review/" class="text-amber-700 font-semibold hover:underline">Compare current Harvia heater formats</a></p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Warranty: read the exclusions and remedies</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Almost Heaven currently advertises a limited lifetime warranty against manufacturing defects on the sauna room. It separately lists one year for heater elements and five years for other heater components.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-8">The company also says the room warranty does not cover normal wear, rot, discoloration, or minor lumber splintering. Read the full warranty that applies on the purchase date. Check who pays shipping, which records are required, whether labor is covered, and how outdoor maintenance affects a claim.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">What to resolve before checkout</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-3 text-stone-700 mb-8">
      <li>Which exact lumber, door, window, finish, heater, controls, and stones are included?</li>
      <li>What are the current interior and bench dimensions, not just the capacity label?</li>
      <li>Which construction and heater manuals apply to this configuration?</li>
      <li>What foundation, drainage, ventilation, and clearance work is required?</li>
      <li>What are the packed dimensions, freight method, unloading responsibility, and current lead time?</li>
      <li>What electrical or chimney work must be finished before assembly?</li>
      <li>What warranty exclusions, maintenance obligations, and shipping costs apply?</li>
    </ol>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="almost_heaven_brand_guide_article_mid"
      heading="Turn the model into a complete project brief"
      description="Capture your site, dimensions, power, delivery access, budget, and timeline before asking a retailer or installer for a written quote."
    />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Where are Almost Heaven saunas made?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">The company says it has manufactured saunas in West Virginia's Greenbrier Valley since 1977. Its current Harvia Collection is described as crafted in Europe, so check the exact product's country of origin.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Do Almost Heaven sauna kits include a heater?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">Almost Heaven says an electric heater is standard with every sauna it sells. The model and controls vary, and select larger outdoor saunas can use wood-burning packages.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">What does the warranty cover?</h3>
        <p class="text-stone-700">The current summary describes limited-lifetime coverage for manufacturing defects in the sauna room, one year for heater elements, and five years for other heater components. Read the full terms and exclusions before purchase.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12 border-t border-stone-200 pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Primary sources</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-600">
        <li><a href="https://almostheaven.com/pages/about-us" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Almost Heaven company history and current product scope</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://almostheaven.com/pages/faq" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Almost Heaven heater and warranty FAQ</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://almostheaven.com/products/pinnacle-4-person-barrel-sauna" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current Pinnacle product page</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://almostheaven.com/products/grandview-4-6-person-canopy-barrel-sauna" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current Grandview product page</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://almostheaven.com/collections/heritage-collection" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current Harvia Collection</a></li>
        <li><a href={pinnacleUrl} rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Current authorized-retailer Pinnacle listing</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-4">Product configurations, pricing, availability, lead times, and warranty terms can change. Recheck the documents tied to the exact order.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Continue planning</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/best-barrel-sauna-kits/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Compare barrel-sauna formats</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/redwood-outdoors-vs-almost-heaven/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Compare Almost Heaven with Redwood Outdoors</a></li>
        <li><a href="/brands/finnish-sauna-builders-review/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Review the Finnish Sauna Builders dealer path</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/barrel-sauna-vs-cabin-sauna/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Barrel versus cabin planning guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-foundation-guide/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Sauna foundation guide</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/sauna-electrical-requirements/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Electrical planning checklist</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
